Z||000000||JohnsFiero||09-02-2000||10:38 AM||||Okay, everything was going great.  Took my baby for emissions and she passed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> with no problems.  Then was driving home and BAM, no electrical.  It was like someone turned off the ignition.  Got pulled over to the side of the road and arranged a tow.  Now, short of the obvious (the battery checks out, battery cables, etc.) where should I start.  TIA. <P>John  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000001||Rodrv6||09-02-2000||01:08 PM||||You might want to check the fusible links.  On the 84's there are two of them that attatch to the starter solonoid.  All of the power to the car goes through these two links.  They tend to get brittle over time and are prone to breaking without much warning.  <P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE||||reg||4
